# LARGE-BUT-BUDGETED counts (hundreds to a couple thousand) on small bodies.
# Auto-generated for the D27 quantifier/bounded-repeat corpus.
# Every expectation is computed directly from python's re module.

# exact large count
pattern a{500}
n ""
m "" 0 500
m "" 0 500
m "" 0 500

# large bounded range
pattern a{200,500}
n "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"
m "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa" 0 200
m "" 0 350
m "" 0 500
m "" 0 500

# large bounded range, lazy
pattern a{200,500}?
n "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"
m "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa" 0 200
m "" 0 200
m "" 0 200
m "" 0 200

# large exact count, two-char body, capturing group
pattern (ab){300}
n ""
m "" 0 600
g 1 598 600
m "" 0 600
g 1 598 600

# large exact count, class body
pattern [ab]{1000}
m "" 0 1000
m "" 0 1000
m "" 0 1000

# large upper bound, single char body
pattern a{1,2000}
m "a" 0 1
m "" 0 1000
m "" 0 2000
m "" 0 2000

# nested variable-length body AT the 64-copy replication cap
pattern (a{1,3}){64}
n "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"
m "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa" 0 192
g 1 189 192
m "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa" 0 192
g 1 189 192

# one past the 64-copy replication cap. It USED to be a clean refusal and the
# `perr` above is what this block pinned; the [ENG-BREP] counter rung makes a
# bounded repeat's emitted size independent of its COUNT (65 body copies become
# K + 65 mod K = 9), so the cap is no longer reached and the pattern COMPILES.
# Re-expected rather than deleted: the direction is the safe one D47's ADDENDUM
# named (refused -> compiled, so nothing shipped changes under anyone), and the
# cells below are the exact analogue of the {64} block above, both verified
# against python re.
#
# The intermediate lengths are deliberately NOT pinned here, and their absence
# is the honest part: at 65..~100 'a's this is an ambiguous decomposition that
# exhausts the step budget (pcrec returns RX_ERR_STEPS in milliseconds; python
# re does not terminate in 20 s), which is known_issues.md K23's territory and
# owned by [M4.6c]. The {64} block avoids the same region for the same reason.
pattern (a{1,3}){65}
n "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"
m "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa" 0 195
g 1 192 195
